      "priority": 1,
      "title": "An extra administrator account to confirm",
      "finding_ids": [
        "ACCT-EXTRA-ADMIN:fde0b291"
      ],
      "explanation": "The scan found a local user account, <computer>\\<account-2>, that has administrator rights, meaning it can change anything on this computer. This is often perfectly normal: many people keep a separate administrator account on purpose, which is actually good practice, or it may belong to another family member or have been created when the computer was set up. It only becomes a concern if you don't recognize it, because an unknown administrator account can be a sign that someone else got into the computer. This scan was not compared with an earlier one, so it can't tell when the account was added. If you know this account, there is nothing to worry about. If you don't, treat it seriously and follow the fix shown for this finding in the report."
    }
